Don't pass a field delta as the view's row_index.

FullcalendarViewPreprocess sets $view->row_index so Views' advancedRender()
knows which result row it is rendering. For the start-date field it sets it to
the *delta* ($i) of the date value instead of the row's index. row_index is
documented and used as an index into $view->result: EntityField::
prepareItemsByDelta() reads $this->view->result[$this->view->row_index] whenever
a delta limit is configured on a multi-value field.

The two only coincide by accident. When a node has more date values than the
view has result rows -- e.g. a weekly series of 17 dates under an exposed filter
that leaves 4 rows -- the lookup fails with a PHP warning
("Undefined array key N" in EntityField.php), once per date, on every render.
With more rows than deltas the lookup silently picks the wrong row instead,
which is harmless only because the row is then unused.

Use the row's own index for every field. Nothing in the preprocess reads the
delta back out of row_index; the per-delta values come from $start_dates[$i].

Filed against fullcalendar_view 5.2.5.

--- a/src/FullcalendarViewPreprocess.php
+++ b/src/FullcalendarViewPreprocess.php
@@ -227,7 +227,9 @@
             foreach ($fields as $name => $field) {
               if (method_exists($field, 'advancedRender')) {
                 // Set the row_index property used by advancedRender function.
-                $field->view->row_index = preg_match('#^' . $start_field . '(_\d+)?$#', $name) ? $i : $row->index;
+                // It is an index into $view->result, so it must be the row's
+                // own index for every field, the start field included.
+                $field->view->row_index = $row->index;
                 $des[$idkey] = $field->advancedRender($row);
               }
             }
